[{"code":"list_still_used","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":13,"col":27},"end":{"line":13,"col":46}},"title":"LIST CHANGED WHILE STILL IN USE","message":"`Dict.insert` changes the dictionary `old` in place, and another use still holds\nits storage.\n\n12|                old = Dict.singleton 1 2\n                   ^^^ this binding keeps the old storage\n13|                changed = Dict.insert old 3 4\n                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the storage is changed here\n14|                Dict.size old + Dict.size changed\n                             ^^^ this use still needs the old storage\n\nChanging the slots or order would also change what the old dictionary observes.\n\nMake an explicit storage copy with `Dict.copy` before this write. Stored values\nremain shared; copy a stored value too if you need to change that value.\n\nTo keep the old storage unchanged, copy it at this use:\n\n13|                changed = Dict.insert (Dict.copy old) 3 4\n\nThis is sharing the code shows: old is read again at 14:17"}]
